I fell into a lava fan.

5116
04:22:17,270 --> 04:22:18,770
And I lost it all.

5117
04:22:19,210 --> 04:22:19,950
I know.

5118
04:22:20,230 --> 04:22:20,670
I know.

5119
04:22:21,530 --> 04:22:23,190
I can't believe it happened.

5120
04:22:27,320 --> 04:22:28,320
What's up, guys?

5121
04:22:31,360 --> 04:22:32,420
She's in my arms.

5122
04:22:33,140 --> 04:22:34,020
She's supporting me.

5123
04:22:34,180 --> 04:22:35,500
She knew I went through something bad.

5124
04:22:37,300 --> 04:22:38,420
Oh, now she jumped off.

5125
04:22:38,580 --> 04:22:38,680
Okay.

5126
04:22:39,600 --> 04:22:41,100
That was the emotional support I got.

5127
04:22:41,840 --> 04:22:42,400
No more.

5128
04:22:48,520 --> 04:22:49,900
At least you didn't lose your pickaxe.

5129
04:22:50,020 --> 04:22:50,740
You're right, I didn't.

5130
04:22:50,920 --> 04:22:51,660
That's actually...

5131
04:22:51,660 --> 04:22:52,080
Thank you.

5132
04:22:52,340 --> 04:22:52,900
Silver lining.

5133
04:22:53,600 --> 04:22:54,100
You're right.

5134
04:22:54,640 --> 04:22:55,700
That's how you should look at it.

5135
04:22:57,340 --> 04:22:58,260
I don't know what I...

5136
04:22:58,780 --> 04:23:03,200
I maybe expected to be set on fire down there, but I didn't expect to immediately die.

5137
04:23:04,240 --> 04:23:06,980
Because I went from 100 to zero in no time.

5138
04:23:07,720 --> 04:23:09,020
You know, I was sort of ready.

5139
04:23:09,120 --> 04:23:10,260
Okay, maybe I'll catch fire.

5140
04:23:10,260 --> 04:23:11,100
I'll jump out, you know?

5141
04:23:12,020 --> 04:23:13,900
But I couldn't even jump out for some reason.

5142
04:23:15,700 --> 04:23:16,960
I learned my lesson, though.

5143
04:23:18,000 --> 04:23:19,360
Dude, I got blasted.

5144
04:23:25,280 --> 04:23:26,340
It's lavaed air.

5145
04:23:26,520 --> 04:23:27,340
That's a good way to put it.

5146
04:23:33,000 --> 04:23:36,040
In hindsight, it wasn't a smart idea to jump into the blaster.

5147
04:23:37,020 --> 04:23:38,340
Just give it the name, you know?

5148
04:23:38,540 --> 04:23:39,340
You don't want to do that.

5149
04:23:40,260 --> 04:23:41,900
I was like, how am I gonna get my item otherwise?

5150
04:23:42,760 --> 04:23:44,960
But there's gotta be a way to extract that item, I imagine.

5151
04:23:45,380 --> 04:23:46,620
A hopper, for example.

5152
04:23:48,480 --> 04:23:49,840
There's many ways to do that.

5153
04:23:54,760 --> 04:23:55,480
Worth a test?

5154
04:23:55,640 --> 04:23:56,500
I think so, yeah.

5155
04:23:56,620 --> 04:23:57,240
I learned my lesson.

5156
04:23:57,340 --> 04:23:58,440
I will never attempt that again.

5157
04:24:00,520 --> 04:24:04,220
By the way, the last S in chassis is silent for whatever reason.

5158
04:24:04,320 --> 04:24:05,260
Okay, so chassis...

5159
04:24:05,260 --> 04:24:05,860
Chassis?

5160
04:24:06,840 --> 04:24:07,920
Chassis?

5161
04:24:07,920 --> 04:24:08,440
Is that how you say it?

5162
04:24:09,940 --> 04:24:10,540
Chassis.

5163
04:24:11,700 --> 04:24:12,300
Chassis.

5164
04:24:12,620 --> 04:24:14,040
It's not chassis, right?

5165
04:24:14,100 --> 04:24:14,580
It's chassis.

5166
04:24:15,600 --> 04:24:16,120
Okay, good.

5167
04:24:17,620 --> 04:24:19,340
The CH is also pronounced...

5168
04:24:20,460 --> 04:24:21,800
Oh, chassis.

5169
04:24:22,320 --> 04:24:22,840
Really?

5170
04:24:23,560 --> 04:24:24,160
Chassis.

5171
04:24:25,060 --> 04:24:25,420
Ah!

5172
04:24:25,900 --> 04:24:26,800
Okay, thank you.

5173
04:24:27,600 --> 04:24:28,580
Learning English.

5174
04:24:29,600 --> 04:24:30,920
I got it, I got it.

5175
04:24:30,980 --> 04:24:32,120
I will never forget it now.

5176
04:24:33,520 --> 04:24:37,560
It's like, I keep saying miscellaneous when it's really miscellaneous.

5177
04:24:40,280 --> 04:24:41,460
Must be my...

5178
04:24:43,160 --> 04:24:44,640
German I learned once in a while.

5179
04:24:44,780 --> 04:24:47,600
They always go shh on things, you know, so that's ingrained in me.

5180
04:24:54,170 --> 04:24:54,490
Miscellaneous.

5181
04:24:54,750 --> 04:24:57,570
Actually, now that I say it like that, it does sound very smooth.

5182
04:24:57,730 --> 04:24:58,590
You know, miscellaneous.

5183
04:24:58,730 --> 04:24:59,790
It's so much easier to say, too.

5184
04:25:01,370 --> 04:25:04,010
So how would you pronounce it if it's like shortened?

5185
04:25:04,350 --> 04:25:04,870
Just mis?

5186
04:25:06,890 --> 04:25:09,110
Because I always think misc.

5187
04:25:10,230 --> 04:25:11,750
But that is totally...

5188
04:25:11,750 --> 04:25:12,610
Yeah, right, misc!

5189
04:25:13,630 --> 04:25:14,590
That's what I do.

5190
04:25:15,990 --> 04:25:16,530
Misk.

5191
04:25:20,840 --> 04:25:22,340
But that doesn't even sound right.

5192
04:25:24,360 --> 04:25:25,780
Oliver, you're a Danish legend.

5193
04:25:26,260 --> 04:25:26,740
Are you?

5194
04:25:27,240 --> 04:25:27,620
I think.

5195
04:25:33,000 --> 04:25:35,260
English makes no sense even to native speakers.

5196
04:25:36,960 --> 04:25:38,540
I think English makes a lot of sense.

5197
04:25:38,800 --> 04:25:40,520
It's one of the few languages that makes sense.

5198
04:25:41,060 --> 04:25:41,980
In a lot of ways.

5199
04:25:43,380 --> 04:25:44,620
But I see what you're talking about.

5200
04:25:44,720 --> 04:25:45,180
I see what you mean.

5201
04:25:47,300 --> 04:25:49,560
I'm at the gym watching your stream between sets.

5202
04:25:51,560 --> 04:25:51,960
How?

5203
04:25:52,440 --> 04:25:53,360
How are you doing that?

5204
04:25:53,400 --> 04:25:54,320
On your phone or something?

5205
04:25:54,320 --> 04:25:56,180
With headphones in or...

5206
04:25:56,180 --> 04:25:57,480
What is your setup like?

5207
04:25:58,100 --> 04:25:58,540
Frigidero.

5208
04:26:05,130 --> 04:26:06,990
I've never been inside a gym in my life.

5209
04:26:08,690 --> 04:26:10,570
It's like this mythical place in my mind.

5210
04:26:11,130 --> 04:26:12,410
I don't even know what it's like.

5211
04:26:14,950 --> 04:26:16,650
Never stepped foot inside a gym.

5212
04:26:19,670 --> 04:26:20,410
Not gym.

5213
04:26:21,750 --> 04:26:23,690
I guess there's no way to pronounce it differently.

5214
04:26:27,300 --> 04:26:27,900
Same here.

5215
04:26:28,020 --> 04:26:28,740
I'm at the gym as well.

5216
04:26:28,880 --> 04:26:29,060
What?

5217
04:26:29,060 --> 04:26:30,480
Why are you guys at the gym?

5218
04:26:31,080 --> 04:26:32,000
Watching me at the gym.

5219
04:26:32,140 --> 04:26:32,720
That's kind of weird.

5220
04:26:33,540 --> 04:26:34,000
Isn't it?

5221
04:26:35,420 --> 04:26:36,580
Just my phone and AirPods?

5222
04:26:36,840 --> 04:26:37,180
Oh, okay.

5223
04:26:38,780 --> 04:26:40,780
I guess that's a dumb question on my part.

5224
04:26:40,880 --> 04:26:41,500
What else would you do?

5225
04:26:41,800 --> 04:26:43,700
It's not like you bring a laptop to the gym.

5226
04:26:44,480 --> 04:26:45,580
Obviously it would be the phone.

5227
04:26:47,340 --> 04:26:48,580
And I hope I'm not on speaker.

5228
04:26:48,700 --> 04:26:49,680
You know, that would be even weirder.

5229
04:26:51,620 --> 04:26:53,720
You're a source of motivation to pull more reps?

5230
04:26:54,300 --> 04:26:54,780
Really?

5231
04:26:56,220 --> 04:26:57,700
Well, I'm glad to be of assistance.

5232
04:26:58,780 --> 04:26:59,840
May you get ripped.

5233
04:27:01,100 --> 04:27:02,220
I wish you all the best.

5234
04:27:06,260 --> 04:27:07,920
I'm not falling for that bait.

5235
04:27:09,380 --> 04:27:09,860
Kedawik.

5236
04:27:10,100 --> 04:27:10,940
Or Kerawik.

5237
04:27:12,580 --> 04:27:13,720
I do like Gears.

5238
04:27:13,860 --> 04:27:14,020
I do like Gears.

5239
04:27:14,780 --> 04:27:15,840
I love the Gears.

5240
04:27:20,720 --> 04:27:21,480
Vintage Story?

5241
04:27:21,560 --> 04:27:22,880
That game is not finished though, right?

5242
04:27:24,040 --> 04:27:25,140
It's still in development.

5243
04:27:27,740 --> 04:27:29,840
Are you gonna release the custom JEI mod?

5244
04:27:29,840 --> 04:27:31,540
There's actually no JEI in it anymore.

5245
04:27:33,100 --> 04:27:34,920
The JEI is completely stripped of it.

5246
04:27:35,640 --> 04:27:38,500
The animations you see and stuff, it's not actually JEI.

5247
04:27:38,640 --> 04:27:39,860
It is native create.

5248
04:27:40,720 --> 04:27:43,420
JEI is just the surface that is using to display it.

5249
04:27:44,940 --> 04:27:45,380
Yeah.

5250
04:27:46,620 --> 04:27:47,640
Maybe at some point.

5251
04:27:53,450 --> 04:27:55,630
People just don't like how the sausage is made, you know?

5252
04:27:55,730 --> 04:27:57,790
So I kinda just wanna keep it to myself.

5253
04:27:58,070 --> 04:27:58,710
For now.

5254
04:27:59,570 --> 04:28:00,270
I think.

5255
04:28:09,670 --> 04:28:12,310
There's like over a hundred unit tests in that mod so far.

5256
04:28:12,710 --> 04:28:15,090
To check that whenever a change is made, nothing gets broken.

5257
04:28:16,050 --> 04:28:18,530
It is actually incredibly solid right now.

5258
04:28:22,750 --> 04:28:24,450
Like, I've been running fucking...

5259
04:28:25,550 --> 04:28:27,090
Simulations of players running through it.

5260
04:28:27,170 --> 04:28:27,870
You know, over 400.

5261
04:28:28,750 --> 04:28:29,790
Just testing shit.

5262
04:28:31,190 --> 04:28:32,530
So I don't have to get spoiled.

5263
04:28:36,610 --> 04:28:37,850
It's kinda nuts.

5264
04:28:38,210 --> 04:28:39,730
I've been going a little too hard on that.

5265
04:28:42,910 --> 04:28:44,190
This dream was so overwhelming.

5266
04:28:45,310 --> 04:28:46,690
At times I can see why.

5267
04:28:46,990 --> 04:28:48,110
I was also overwhelmed.

5268
04:28:48,290 --> 04:28:49,290
We can be overwhelmed together.

5269
04:28:53,670 --> 04:28:55,150
Could you say a Danish tongue twister?

5270
04:28:55,190 --> 04:28:55,970
It would be very funny.

5271
04:28:57,530 --> 04:28:57,930
Uh...

5272
04:28:59,970 --> 04:29:00,750
That's a good one.

5273
04:29:00,890 --> 04:29:01,610
Very common one.

5274
04:29:02,410 --> 04:29:02,990
Or you can say...

5275
04:29:07,310 --> 04:29:09,130
Which is like a very long word in Danish.

5276
04:29:10,030 --> 04:29:11,050
Nobody uses that word.

5277
04:29:11,210 --> 04:29:11,750
But it is a thing.

5278
04:29:13,410 --> 04:29:14,730
Or you can say...

5279
04:29:18,810 --> 04:29:19,710
Oh, I got them all.

5280
04:29:20,890 --> 04:29:22,050
I had that on command.

5281
04:29:23,490 --> 04:29:23,970
What?

5282
04:29:25,730 --> 04:29:25,990
Exactly.

5283
04:29:26,510 --> 04:29:27,070
You got it.

5284
04:29:29,470 --> 04:29:30,630
What does the word mean?

5285
04:29:30,930 --> 04:29:31,410
I...

5286
04:29:31,410 --> 04:29:32,710
It's apparently a job.

5287
04:29:32,830 --> 04:29:33,690
Or was a job.

5288
04:29:35,350 --> 04:29:37,930
Imagine having that job and being asked what you do for a job.

5289
04:29:38,990 --> 04:29:40,570
I would hate being asked that question.

5290
04:29:43,890 --> 04:29:45,130
You're just making sounds, right?

5291
04:29:45,770 --> 04:29:47,070
I mean, isn't that what language is?

5292
04:29:48,510 --> 04:29:49,790
Those are actual words.

5293
04:29:49,910 --> 04:29:51,330
The Danish people in chat will confirm.

5294
04:29:53,490 --> 04:29:54,910
I work with people.

5295
04:29:55,270 --> 04:29:55,830
Exactly.

5296
04:29:56,110 --> 04:29:56,650
That's a good answer.

5297
04:30:03,600 --> 04:30:05,740
It sounds so normal to hear you talk Danish.

5298
04:30:05,780 --> 04:30:07,140
It's like you're just a regular guy.

5299
04:30:07,720 --> 04:30:09,860
Well, I am a regular guy.

5300
04:30:10,780 --> 04:30:13,480
I am so regular, you don't even understand.

5301
04:30:14,420 --> 04:30:15,900
I'm extremely regular.

5302
04:30:21,530 --> 04:30:23,870
